# {{name}}

A spektr exec module ({{lang}}). It looks up a username and reports the account it finds.

```
spektr module test ./{{name}} --input username:<a handle you may look up>   # live, validated
spektr module test ./{{name}} --input username:<handle> --record             # save a fixture
spektr module test ./{{name}} --fixture fixtures/username_example.jsonl --input username:example
spektr module check ./{{name}}
spektr module install ./{{name}}
```

- `module.toml` declares what it consumes and produces, its hosts and secrets (MODULES §2).
- Messages follow the exec protocol (MODULES §3): every entity, edge and attr cites an observation.
- `fixtures/` holds recorded runs; `check` replays every one through validation.

Only look up people and accounts you're allowed to.
